1
00:00:00,667 --> 00:00:04,879
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10,927 --> 00:00:12,637
<i>I have a feeling she's suspicious of you.</i>

3
00:00:12,721 --> 00:00:15,140
<i>She could be planning something.</i>

4
00:00:15,223 --> 00:00:18,518
<i>I'll send my men there to abduct Ivy</i>

5
00:00:18,601 --> 00:00:21,354
<i>and bring her to my happy place.</i>

6
00:00:21,438 --> 00:00:24,023
[Arnaldo] <i>I trust her, Grandpa.</i>
<i>She'd never betray me.</i>

7
00:00:24,107 --> 00:00:28,820
<i>Have you committed murder because of love?</i>

8
00:00:28,903 --> 00:00:33,950
<i>Grandpa taught me to use my brain</i>
<i>over my emotions.</i>

9
00:00:34,034 --> 00:00:36,703
<i>If you let emotion take over,</i>
<i>you might end up killing someone.</i>

10
00:00:36,786 --> 00:00:39,330
[Ivy] <i>Your death isn't payment enough</i>

11
00:00:39,414 --> 00:00:41,041
<i>for what you did.</i>

12
00:00:41,124 --> 00:00:43,752
<i>I won't let you off that easily, Arnaldo.</i>

13
00:00:43,835 --> 00:00:47,714
<i>I won't taint my hands</i>
<i>with blood for someone like you.</i>

14
00:00:47,797 --> 00:00:49,758
[Raul] <i>Right now, I'm in</i>
<i>control of the situation.</i>

15
00:00:49,841 --> 00:00:52,635
<i>So, I can provide everything you need.</i>

16
00:00:52,719 --> 00:00:54,512
<i>But you have to give me what I need too.</i>

17
00:00:54,596 --> 00:00:57,057
<i>We must rise above our fears!</i>

18
00:00:57,140 --> 00:01:00,769
<i>They cannot oppress us if we are united!</i>

19
00:01:00,852 --> 00:01:02,437
<i>Long live the new Ardiente!</i>

20
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:03,438
[all] <i>Long live!</i>

21
00:01:03,521 --> 00:01:04,481
[applause]

22
00:01:04,564 --> 00:01:05,982
<i>It's from a certain Jaguar.</i>

23
00:01:06,066 --> 00:01:08,109
<i>They want to enter the gambling scene</i>
<i>here in Ardiente.</i>

24
00:01:08,693 --> 00:01:11,404
[Julio] <i>Kittens aren't welcome</i>
<i>in my business.</i>

25
00:01:11,488 --> 00:01:12,363
[gunshot]

26
00:01:12,447 --> 00:01:15,325
<i>Tell the congressman</i>
<i>that the Jaguar is here.</i>

27
00:01:15,408 --> 00:01:17,702
<i>And he will rule Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

28
00:01:17,786 --> 00:01:19,954
[Diego] <i>Ivy, I just want to</i>
<i>make sure you're safe.</i>

29
00:01:20,038 --> 00:01:22,207
<i>I won't do anything that'll get me killed.</i>

30
00:01:22,290 --> 00:01:23,792
<i>I can protect myself.</i>

31
00:01:23,875 --> 00:01:26,085
[Diego] <i>If you need me,</i>
<i>you know where to find me.</i>

32
00:01:26,169 --> 00:01:27,837
<i>I'm done playing your games.</i>

33
00:01:27,921 --> 00:01:29,589
<i>-Arnaldo, wait!</i>
<i>-What?! Explain yourself!</i>

34
00:01:29,672 --> 00:01:30,632
<i>Listen to me.</i>

35
00:01:30,715 --> 00:01:33,009
<i>Give me one good reason</i>
<i>why I need to stay!</i>

36
00:01:33,092 --> 00:01:34,135
<i>I love you.</i>

37
00:01:34,219 --> 00:01:36,888
<i>Stay, Arnaldo. I love you.</i>

38
00:01:41,893 --> 00:01:43,937
[suspenseful music playing]

39
00:01:44,020 --> 00:01:45,563
[knocks on door]

40
00:01:46,648 --> 00:01:47,649
Come in.

41
00:01:48,358 --> 00:01:50,151
Excuse me, Congressman.

42
00:01:53,113 --> 00:01:58,785
[suspenseful music playing]

43
00:02:19,055 --> 00:02:23,601
[suspenseful music playing]

44
00:02:25,061 --> 00:02:27,188
<i>Honorable Congressman,</i>

45
00:02:27,272 --> 00:02:29,607
<i>Sorry about killing your men,</i>

46
00:02:29,691 --> 00:02:31,484
<i>but they were getting too cocky.</i>

47
00:02:31,568 --> 00:02:34,904
<i>That's why I'm advising you</i>
<i>to have some coffee.</i>

48
00:02:35,446 --> 00:02:38,533
<i>Because if I find you</i>
<i>getting too cocky as well,</i>

49
00:02:38,616 --> 00:02:41,786
<i>I'll put a bullet through your head.</i>

50
00:02:42,412 --> 00:02:44,914
<i>Love, Jaguar.</i>

51
00:02:48,209 --> 00:02:52,547
[suspenseful music playing]

52
00:02:59,178 --> 00:03:01,097
Okay, I'll admit.

53
00:03:03,141 --> 00:03:04,267
I admit that…

54
00:03:04,809 --> 00:03:06,853
Diego and I still see each other.

55
00:03:07,812 --> 00:03:09,689
But I told him to stay away.

56
00:03:10,899 --> 00:03:13,318
Because I know I'm sure of…

57
00:03:14,068 --> 00:03:15,695
my feelings for you.

58
00:03:16,905 --> 00:03:20,617
I'm testing the depth
of your feelings for me.

59
00:03:21,743 --> 00:03:23,995
Arnaldo, I'm not playing you.

60
00:03:24,537 --> 00:03:26,623
I'm not toying with you.

61
00:03:27,582 --> 00:03:29,542
I love you, and I hope…

62
00:03:30,293 --> 00:03:32,879
I hope that's enough for you to stay.

63
00:03:35,256 --> 00:03:36,341
I love you.

64
00:03:37,759 --> 00:03:39,469
I love you, Arnaldo.

65
00:03:39,552 --> 00:03:43,848
[tense music playing]

66
00:03:45,892 --> 00:03:47,060
It's more than enough.

67
00:03:47,644 --> 00:03:49,187
More than enough reason.

68
00:03:50,897 --> 00:03:55,526
[tense music playing]

69
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:03,826
I've been loving you for so long.

70
00:04:04,619 --> 00:04:05,954
[exhales]

71
00:04:12,252 --> 00:04:13,795
Arnaldo…

72
00:04:17,715 --> 00:04:18,883
[exhales]

73
00:04:23,805 --> 00:04:24,806
[Arnaldo] Ouch!

74
00:04:24,889 --> 00:04:26,307
-Does it hurt?
-Please be gentle.

75
00:04:26,391 --> 00:04:27,392
It hurts.

76
00:04:27,725 --> 00:04:28,726
Sorry.

77
00:04:29,477 --> 00:04:31,312
You're so cute, you know?

78
00:04:31,396 --> 00:04:32,855
You're way cuter.

79
00:04:33,815 --> 00:04:35,483
-[Arnaldo chuckles]
-Arnaldo…

80
00:04:39,904 --> 00:04:42,240
But seriously, thank you
for taking care of me.

81
00:04:45,702 --> 00:04:46,744
I love you.

82
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:50,206
I love you.

83
00:04:59,007 --> 00:05:00,550
[phone ringing]

84
00:05:00,633 --> 00:05:02,218
-[phone ringing]
-[Arnaldo groans]

85
00:05:02,302 --> 00:05:04,262
-Bad timing.
-[phone ringing]

86
00:05:04,345 --> 00:05:06,431
Sorry, I have to take this. It's Grandpa.

87
00:05:06,514 --> 00:05:08,016
-Hello, Grandpa?
-<i>Arnaldo.</i>

88
00:05:08,725 --> 00:05:10,268
Come home right now.

89
00:05:10,727 --> 00:05:12,061
Huh? But why?

90
00:05:13,730 --> 00:05:16,566
Somebody new picked a fight
with our family.

91
00:05:17,942 --> 00:05:22,196
[ominous music playing]

92
00:05:30,830 --> 00:05:33,499
Leave everything right there. Thank you.

93
00:05:33,583 --> 00:05:34,542
You're welcome, ma'am.

94
00:05:34,625 --> 00:05:36,085
We'll return to our posts now.

95
00:05:36,169 --> 00:05:38,087
Okay. Have some snacks too.

96
00:05:38,171 --> 00:05:39,297
Thank you, ma'am.

97
00:05:41,549 --> 00:05:43,843
Um, Nimfa?

98
00:05:44,177 --> 00:05:46,262
Leave everything here. You can go home.

99
00:05:46,345 --> 00:05:48,264
Your parents might be looking for you.

100
00:05:48,347 --> 00:05:51,142
Oh, it's okay, Miss Camia.

101
00:05:51,225 --> 00:05:54,854
You see, my father isn't around.

102
00:05:54,937 --> 00:05:56,397
He's in Manila.

103
00:05:56,481 --> 00:06:00,318
Besides, I'm sure he'll be happy
once he finds out

104
00:06:00,401 --> 00:06:03,738
that I'm helping the bravest
opponent of the Ardientes.

105
00:06:03,821 --> 00:06:05,114
[Nimfa chuckles]

106
00:06:06,074 --> 00:06:07,784
Where's your mother?

107
00:06:09,869 --> 00:06:11,621
[sighs] She's gone.

108
00:06:17,043 --> 00:06:19,420
Um… Miss Camia?

109
00:06:20,379 --> 00:06:22,381
Don't you have any helpers around?

110
00:06:23,633 --> 00:06:25,134
They took the day off.

111
00:06:26,010 --> 00:06:27,345
I see.

112
00:06:27,428 --> 00:06:31,474
Wait, so who does the chores for you?

113
00:06:31,557 --> 00:06:32,850
No one.

114
00:06:32,934 --> 00:06:34,143
I grew up poor.

115
00:06:34,227 --> 00:06:35,895
I can do everything on my own.

116
00:06:35,978 --> 00:06:37,980
But you have so many things to do.

117
00:06:38,064 --> 00:06:39,649
You might overwork yourself.

118
00:06:41,067 --> 00:06:42,318
All right, then.

119
00:06:42,401 --> 00:06:45,363
I'll do the household chores myself.

120
00:06:45,446 --> 00:06:48,866
I can do everything! All around!

121
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:51,744
Don't worry, you don't have to pay me.

122
00:06:51,828 --> 00:06:54,288
-Goodness.
-I'll be your volunteer helper.

123
00:06:54,372 --> 00:06:56,707
Nimfa, you don't have to.

124
00:06:56,791 --> 00:06:59,627
But, Miss Camia, that's what I want to do.

125
00:07:00,253 --> 00:07:02,338
Come on, let me do it.

126
00:07:02,421 --> 00:07:03,422
Please?

127
00:07:03,798 --> 00:07:04,841
No.

128
00:07:04,924 --> 00:07:05,800
[sighs]

129
00:07:05,883 --> 00:07:07,552
-[Camia chuckles]
-[phone ringing]

130
00:07:08,010 --> 00:07:09,887
Hold on. I have to answer this.

131
00:07:09,971 --> 00:07:11,222
-Okay, ma'am.
-[phone ringing]

132
00:07:17,645 --> 00:07:18,688
Hello?

133
00:07:19,105 --> 00:07:20,189
Lily.

134
00:07:21,607 --> 00:07:22,859
You're going home already?

135
00:07:23,484 --> 00:07:24,610
But why?

136
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:29,740
Okay, dear. Stay safe
on your way home, okay?

137
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:32,785
Okay. Bye.

138
00:07:33,661 --> 00:07:37,582
[unsettling music playing]

139
00:07:42,503 --> 00:07:45,840
["Wildflower" by Arnel Pineda playing]

140
00:07:58,436 --> 00:08:04,692
<i>♪ She's faced the hardest times</i>
<i>You can imagine ♪</i>

141
00:08:04,775 --> 00:08:11,741
<i>♪ And many times</i>
<i>Her eyes fought back the tears ♪</i>

142
00:08:12,867 --> 00:08:18,372
<i>♪ And when her youthful world</i>
<i>Was about to fall in ♪</i>

143
00:08:18,456 --> 00:08:25,463
<i>♪ Each time her slender shoulders</i>
<i>Bore the weight of all her fears… ♪</i>

144
00:08:25,546 --> 00:08:28,216
<i>You'll always be in my heart,</i>
<i>Nanny Carlotta.</i>

145
00:08:29,675 --> 00:08:32,136
<i>I'll continue our fight.</i>

146
00:08:33,054 --> 00:08:35,306
<i>I'll find justice for your death.</i>

147
00:08:36,015 --> 00:08:38,518
<i>♪ Let her cry ♪</i>

148
00:08:38,601 --> 00:08:42,104
<i>♪ For she's a lady ♪</i>

149
00:08:42,980 --> 00:08:46,943
<i>♪ Let her dream ♪</i>

150
00:08:47,026 --> 00:08:49,695
<i>♪ She's a child ♪</i>

151
00:08:49,779 --> 00:08:51,197
<i>♪ Let the rain… ♪</i>

152
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:54,867
<i>Nanny Carlotta. I've laid down the trap.</i>

153
00:08:54,951 --> 00:08:59,330
<i>All we need is for him</i>
<i>to walk right into it.</i>

154
00:09:00,039 --> 00:09:02,250
[Carlotta] <i>Jepoy is gone.</i>

155
00:09:02,333 --> 00:09:04,585
<i>No one else is going to protect you.</i>

156
00:09:06,045 --> 00:09:07,129
[Diego] <i>I will.</i>

157
00:09:09,131 --> 00:09:11,008
<i>I'll protect Ivy.</i>

158
00:09:16,097 --> 00:09:18,391
[Diego] <i>Ivy, I just want to</i>
<i>make sure you're safe.</i>

159
00:09:18,474 --> 00:09:20,851
[Ivy] <i>I won't do anything</i>
<i>that'll get me killed.</i>

160
00:09:21,310 --> 00:09:22,895
<i>I can protect myself.</i>

161
00:09:22,979 --> 00:09:26,274
<i>If you need me, you know where to find me.</i>

162
00:09:26,691 --> 00:09:28,317
<i>Ivy, be careful.</i>

163
00:09:39,161 --> 00:09:45,001
<i>♪ Be careful how you touch her</i>
<i>For she'll awaken ♪</i>

164
00:09:45,084 --> 00:09:52,091
<i>♪ And sleep's the only freedom</i>
<i>That she knows ♪</i>

165
00:09:53,426 --> 00:09:59,181
<i>♪ And when you walk into her eyes</i>
<i>You won't believe ♪</i>

166
00:09:59,265 --> 00:10:05,187
<i>♪ The way she's always paying</i>
<i>For a debt she never owes ♪</i>

167
00:10:06,981 --> 00:10:10,401
[suspenseful music playing]

168
00:10:12,486 --> 00:10:13,362
Jaguar!

169
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:36,344
[suspenseful music playing]

170
00:10:40,806 --> 00:10:42,516
[Jaguar] There's more
where that came from.

171
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:45,102
We'll take all of the Ardientes' money.

172
00:10:45,186 --> 00:10:46,687
We'll milk them dry.

173
00:10:47,438 --> 00:10:48,648
[goon] For the Jaguar!

174
00:10:49,065 --> 00:10:50,441
[goons] Jaguar!

175
00:10:52,276 --> 00:10:53,653
Oh, Miss Camia!

176
00:10:53,736 --> 00:10:55,738
Nimfa, what are you doing here?

177
00:10:55,821 --> 00:10:57,907
I brought you some lunch

178
00:10:57,990 --> 00:10:59,659
so that you wouldn't have to cook.

179
00:10:59,742 --> 00:11:02,244
Here, I have some vegetables and fish.

180
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:06,123
I'm sorry, that's all I've got…

181
00:11:06,207 --> 00:11:08,000
It's all I can afford.

182
00:11:08,084 --> 00:11:10,711
Nimfa, you shouldn't have!

183
00:11:10,795 --> 00:11:13,172
You don't have to do this.

184
00:11:13,547 --> 00:11:14,548
[chuckles]

185
00:11:14,632 --> 00:11:16,967
Well, I like being thoughtful to you.

186
00:11:18,094 --> 00:11:22,181
But, what if tell you to
stop being thoughtful?

187
00:11:22,264 --> 00:11:23,307
Will you stop?

188
00:11:23,391 --> 00:11:24,433
Hmm…

189
00:11:24,517 --> 00:11:25,518
No, ma'am.

190
00:11:25,601 --> 00:11:28,396
I really want to work
as your house helper.

191
00:11:28,479 --> 00:11:29,271
What?

192
00:11:29,355 --> 00:11:31,899
Please, Miss Camia let me work for you.

193
00:11:31,982 --> 00:11:33,109
-Oh, Nimfa.
-Please.

194
00:11:33,192 --> 00:11:35,611
-Nimfa, get up!
-Let me work for you.

195
00:11:36,153 --> 00:11:37,154
Oh, Nimfa…

196
00:11:37,238 --> 00:11:39,156
Why are you doing this?

197
00:11:40,616 --> 00:11:41,867
[sighs]

198
00:11:42,993 --> 00:11:44,120
Because…

199
00:11:45,538 --> 00:11:47,832
I see my mother in you.

200
00:11:49,041 --> 00:11:52,169
[soft music playing]

201
00:11:53,337 --> 00:11:57,091
[suspenseful music playing]

202
00:11:57,174 --> 00:12:00,136
[phone ringing]

203
00:12:01,554 --> 00:12:02,430
[Rufo] Hello, boss?

204
00:12:05,349 --> 00:12:06,350
Okay.

205
00:12:09,353 --> 00:12:11,856
Jaguar, the boss wants to talk to you.

206
00:12:14,442 --> 00:12:19,613
[suspenseful music playing]

207
00:12:30,249 --> 00:12:34,587
[tense music playing]

208
00:12:36,005 --> 00:12:37,882
Papa, you wanted to see us?

209
00:12:37,965 --> 00:12:39,508
Yes, sit down.

210
00:12:42,761 --> 00:12:44,805
I want everyone here listening.

211
00:12:44,889 --> 00:12:46,640
Including me, Papa?

212
00:12:48,142 --> 00:12:50,311
I'm not in a joking mood, Raul.

213
00:12:50,769 --> 00:12:51,854
Sit down and listen.

214
00:12:51,937 --> 00:12:55,274
[tense music playing]

215
00:12:55,357 --> 00:12:56,442
[heavy sigh]

216
00:12:57,902 --> 00:12:59,820
-Good morning, Grandpa.
-You're late.

217
00:13:02,156 --> 00:13:03,657
What happened to your neck?

218
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:05,743
This? Nothing, I'm okay.

219
00:13:06,619 --> 00:13:08,370
So, we're all here.

220
00:13:08,454 --> 00:13:10,873
-What's this meeting for?
-Sit down.

221
00:13:14,835 --> 00:13:18,923
An armed group of men
broke into our gambling den.

222
00:13:20,382 --> 00:13:23,802
They took over our operations,

223
00:13:23,886 --> 00:13:25,930
they took our money,

224
00:13:26,013 --> 00:13:29,016
and they killed our people.

225
00:13:30,518 --> 00:13:34,146
And the leader of this
group calls himself…

226
00:13:34,230 --> 00:13:35,231
Jaguar.

227
00:13:36,148 --> 00:13:37,274
Jaguar?

228
00:13:37,691 --> 00:13:38,817
[Julio sighs]

229
00:13:39,151 --> 00:13:42,821
[tense music playing]

230
00:13:44,114 --> 00:13:45,616
HOW'S MY HANDSOME MAYOR?
I MISS YOU!

231
00:13:46,325 --> 00:13:47,368
[Julio] Now, listen.

232
00:13:48,077 --> 00:13:50,329
I have had many encounters

233
00:13:50,412 --> 00:13:53,707
and many threats in my political career.

234
00:13:54,208 --> 00:13:56,877
But, I'm telling you,
this group is different.

235
00:13:56,961 --> 00:13:59,505
This group is dangerous.

236
00:13:59,964 --> 00:14:01,549
They're fearless.

237
00:14:01,632 --> 00:14:03,759
They have weapons, they--

238
00:14:05,761 --> 00:14:07,972
Arnaldo, are you listening to me?

239
00:14:08,055 --> 00:14:10,015
-Oh--
-Put that phone down!

240
00:14:10,849 --> 00:14:11,976
Yes.

241
00:14:12,977 --> 00:14:15,312
I want you to focus on this enemy!

242
00:14:17,481 --> 00:14:21,986
Use your informants! Use
your people! Spread the word!

243
00:14:23,529 --> 00:14:27,032
I'm willing to give
10 million pesos as a reward

244
00:14:27,116 --> 00:14:32,454
to whoever can tell me
who and where that Jaguar is.

245
00:14:33,622 --> 00:14:37,710
[tense music playing]

246
00:14:38,794 --> 00:14:40,129
Please, Miss Camia!

247
00:14:40,212 --> 00:14:44,216
I'll be the happiest
if you let me work for you.

248
00:14:44,300 --> 00:14:46,594
So, please… Let me!

249
00:14:46,677 --> 00:14:47,928
Please!

250
00:14:48,304 --> 00:14:49,388
-Please, ma'am!
-[Camia chuckles]

251
00:14:49,471 --> 00:14:50,848
Please say yes!

252
00:14:50,931 --> 00:14:52,933
Please, ma'am!

253
00:14:53,017 --> 00:14:54,435
All right.

254
00:14:54,518 --> 00:14:57,062
But you can't live here.
You have to head home.

255
00:14:57,146 --> 00:14:58,898
Yes, I promise!

256
00:14:58,981 --> 00:15:01,859
And you'll follow every security rule.

257
00:15:01,942 --> 00:15:03,402
I will! Thank you, Miss Camia!

258
00:15:03,485 --> 00:15:06,488
-Thank you so much.
-Okay, you're hired.

259
00:15:06,572 --> 00:15:07,907
You can start right now.

260
00:15:07,990 --> 00:15:10,534
-Thank you so much.
-You're welcome.

261
00:15:10,618 --> 00:15:13,537
-[phone ringing]
-Sorry, Miss Camia.

262
00:15:13,621 --> 00:15:15,039
I have to take this call.

263
00:15:15,122 --> 00:15:17,249
-It might be my dad.
-Okay, take the call.

264
00:15:17,333 --> 00:15:18,918
Come find me when you're done.

265
00:15:19,001 --> 00:15:20,294
-Okay.
-All right.

266
00:15:20,377 --> 00:15:22,630
-Thanks again, Miss Camia.
-No problem.

267
00:15:23,631 --> 00:15:25,090
-Thank you!
-[phone ringing]

268
00:15:25,758 --> 00:15:27,009
[sighs]

269
00:15:27,092 --> 00:15:31,221
[heavy breathing]

270
00:15:32,556 --> 00:15:37,561
[ominous music playing]

271
00:15:38,062 --> 00:15:39,104
Hello.

272
00:15:41,106 --> 00:15:42,191
Yes.

273
00:15:42,942 --> 00:15:44,276
I'm inside the house.

274
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:48,822
All right.

275
00:15:48,906 --> 00:15:52,409
[ominous music playing]

276
00:15:53,744 --> 00:15:56,246
This is what I've always feared.

277
00:15:58,332 --> 00:16:00,709
I don't understand
why you're threatened by Jaguar.

278
00:16:00,793 --> 00:16:03,253
He doesn't even have the balls
to show his face.

279
00:16:03,921 --> 00:16:06,632
I'm not talking about the Jaguar!

280
00:16:08,175 --> 00:16:09,593
You, Arnaldo!

281
00:16:10,135 --> 00:16:12,805
You've lost focus on your mission

282
00:16:12,888 --> 00:16:16,225
to be the heir to this family's throne.

283
00:16:16,308 --> 00:16:18,477
And all because of that woman!

284
00:16:18,560 --> 00:16:21,230
"That woman." "That woman."
Here we go again.

285
00:16:21,313 --> 00:16:22,398
Grandpa…

286
00:16:23,273 --> 00:16:25,943
My whole life I've served this family.

287
00:16:26,026 --> 00:16:27,653
Since the start, I've done nothing

288
00:16:27,736 --> 00:16:29,071
but try to win your approval.

289
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:32,449
Just this once, let me be happy.

290
00:16:33,325 --> 00:16:34,451
And I'll prove to you

291
00:16:34,535 --> 00:16:36,370
that I'll be a better man because of her.

292
00:16:37,413 --> 00:16:39,039
Don't say it.

293
00:16:39,790 --> 00:16:40,791
Do it!

294
00:16:41,417 --> 00:16:45,212
Ivy Aguas is only an asset to this family

295
00:16:45,295 --> 00:16:47,464
because of her money.

296
00:16:48,048 --> 00:16:49,466
And she becomes a problem

297
00:16:49,550 --> 00:16:53,012
when you let your stupid heart
get ahead of you!

298
00:16:53,095 --> 00:16:54,847
And that makes you selfish!

299
00:16:54,930 --> 00:16:56,515
What do you want me to do?

300
00:16:57,016 --> 00:16:58,183
Tell me.

301
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:01,770
You really want her that bad?

302
00:17:01,854 --> 00:17:04,064
Then you go out there and get her!

303
00:17:05,524 --> 00:17:06,900
But make sure

304
00:17:07,443 --> 00:17:09,194
that the whole family

305
00:17:09,278 --> 00:17:12,364
benefits from her assets and money.

306
00:17:13,323 --> 00:17:16,410
What is hers should be ours!

307
00:17:16,493 --> 00:17:18,662
And what is ours

308
00:17:18,746 --> 00:17:21,290
will never be hers.

309
00:17:21,957 --> 00:17:24,960
Do you understand what I'm saying?!

310
00:17:26,837 --> 00:17:30,632
[tense music playing]

311
00:17:40,642 --> 00:17:42,352
[phone ringing]

312
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:49,068
Yes, Mr. Mayor?

313
00:17:49,151 --> 00:17:51,070
I was just thinking about you.

314
00:17:51,862 --> 00:17:53,072
I want to see you.

315
00:17:53,614 --> 00:17:55,199
I have something important to say.

316
00:17:55,282 --> 00:17:56,241
Sure.

317
00:17:56,325 --> 00:17:59,119
Just tell me where and when,
and I'll be there.

318
00:17:59,203 --> 00:18:03,082
[ominous music playing]

319
00:18:12,716 --> 00:18:13,967
Miss Aguas…

320
00:18:15,177 --> 00:18:16,720
Welcome to my playground.

321
00:18:17,805 --> 00:18:20,057
Is that why you brought me here?

322
00:18:20,140 --> 00:18:22,059
You want to play around, Mr. Mayor?

323
00:18:22,684 --> 00:18:23,685
Well…

324
00:18:24,311 --> 00:18:26,522
I'd like to see how good your shot is.

325
00:18:27,606 --> 00:18:28,899
Have you forgotten?

326
00:18:28,982 --> 00:18:30,859
I already showed you how good I am.

327
00:18:33,195 --> 00:18:34,613
[gunshots]

328
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:36,406
[gunshots]

329
00:18:37,825 --> 00:18:42,746
[sultry music playing]

330
00:18:47,334 --> 00:18:48,210
Yes, you're good.

331
00:18:51,338 --> 00:18:53,132
You're good at making lucky shots.

332
00:18:53,590 --> 00:18:55,968
Lucky shots? Really?

333
00:18:57,761 --> 00:18:59,346
Okay, then. Prove me wrong.

334
00:19:00,639 --> 00:19:02,683
Prove to me you belong in my world.

335
00:19:03,976 --> 00:19:06,812
Whoever hits all targets in
the shortest amount of time…

336
00:19:07,437 --> 00:19:08,480
wins.

337
00:19:09,106 --> 00:19:10,482
And what's the prize?

338
00:19:11,358 --> 00:19:12,609
It's a surprise.

339
00:19:13,694 --> 00:19:14,736
Here you go.

340
00:19:16,363 --> 00:19:18,907
[tense music playing]

341
00:19:33,297 --> 00:19:36,550
[tense music playing]

342
00:19:47,895 --> 00:19:48,854
Ready?

343
00:19:51,398 --> 00:19:52,441
Ready?!

344
00:19:53,984 --> 00:19:54,985
Go.

345
00:19:57,154 --> 00:20:00,991
-[action music playing]
-[gunshots]

346
00:20:02,326 --> 00:20:05,829
[gunshots]

347
00:20:14,046 --> 00:20:15,130
[gunshot]

348
00:20:16,131 --> 00:20:17,549
[gunshots]

349
00:20:21,553 --> 00:20:23,931
[gunshots]

350
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:30,020
[unsettling music playing]

351
00:20:40,656 --> 00:20:43,075
[Arnaldo clapping]

352
00:20:47,663 --> 00:20:49,164
Congratulations, Ivy.

353
00:20:50,874 --> 00:20:52,042
You won.

354
00:20:53,710 --> 00:20:54,836
And this…

355
00:20:55,254 --> 00:20:56,713
This is your prize.

356
00:20:59,383 --> 00:21:02,010
A lifetime of love and happiness…

357
00:21:02,094 --> 00:21:03,136
with me.

358
00:21:03,220 --> 00:21:07,557
[unsettling music playing]

359
00:21:07,641 --> 00:21:08,809
Ivy Aguas…

360
00:21:13,313 --> 00:21:14,356
I love you.

361
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:19,569
Will you marry me?

362
00:21:25,617 --> 00:21:30,580
[tense music playing]

363
00:21:30,664 --> 00:21:31,707
"No" isn't an option?

364
00:21:32,124 --> 00:21:33,500
You should know by now

365
00:21:33,583 --> 00:21:35,502
I don't take "no" for an answer.

366
00:21:42,884 --> 00:21:45,595
[tense music playing]

367
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:48,265
Yes.

368
00:21:49,516 --> 00:21:51,935
Yes, Arnaldo. I will marry you.

369
00:21:52,853 --> 00:21:54,229
Yes, Arnaldo.

370
00:21:56,273 --> 00:21:57,482
Your hand, please?

371
00:21:57,566 --> 00:22:00,777
[tense music playing]

372
00:22:00,861 --> 00:22:01,987
[chuckles]

373
00:22:06,283 --> 00:22:09,411
<i>How will I bring the Ardientes down?</i>

374
00:22:09,995 --> 00:22:15,083
<i>Step one: make their favorite</i>
<i>grandson fall for me,</i>

375
00:22:15,167 --> 00:22:18,253
<i>and use him against them.</i>

376
00:22:19,421 --> 00:22:20,380
[fake chuckles]

377
00:22:20,464 --> 00:22:21,631
Arnaldo…

378
00:22:23,633 --> 00:22:24,551
Yes!

379
00:22:24,634 --> 00:22:26,303
-[Ivy forces a laugh]
-[Arnaldo chuckles]

380
00:22:27,137 --> 00:22:28,138
Whoo!

381
00:22:28,764 --> 00:22:30,724
I'm so lucky. Thank you.

382
00:22:30,807 --> 00:22:32,684
Thank you very much for saying yes.

383
00:22:33,351 --> 00:22:34,561
Don't sound so cocky.

384
00:22:35,896 --> 00:22:36,938
You never know.

385
00:22:37,522 --> 00:22:38,648
This?

386
00:22:38,732 --> 00:22:41,485
You've already seen
how good I am at shooting.

387
00:22:42,069 --> 00:22:43,361
Well, don't worry, hon.

388
00:22:43,445 --> 00:22:44,696
I love challenges.

389
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:46,281
Wait, "hon"?

390
00:22:46,364 --> 00:22:47,449
What's wrong?

391
00:22:47,532 --> 00:22:49,743
From now on, that will be
our term of endearment.

392
00:22:50,494 --> 00:22:52,370
My fiancé is so lame.

393
00:22:52,454 --> 00:22:54,456
Well, you can't blame a man in love.

394
00:22:55,499 --> 00:22:57,334
So, I'm okay with it.

395
00:22:58,210 --> 00:23:00,504
Anyway, I can't wait
to tell this to my family.

396
00:23:00,587 --> 00:23:02,631
I'm sure they'll be happy for us.

397
00:23:02,714 --> 00:23:06,176
I'll set a dinner
to announce this to everyone.

398
00:23:11,139 --> 00:23:12,516
You know, Emilia?

399
00:23:12,599 --> 00:23:14,559
Your dad surprised me.

400
00:23:14,643 --> 00:23:18,647
I've known him for a long time,

401
00:23:18,730 --> 00:23:21,525
but this is the first time I've heard him

402
00:23:21,608 --> 00:23:23,610
put a 10-million bounty
on an enemy's head.

403
00:23:23,693 --> 00:23:25,153
It's a huge amount of money.

404
00:23:25,737 --> 00:23:29,282
Well, it only goes to show
he's not taking things lightly.

405
00:23:30,909 --> 00:23:33,286
Do you think he's afraid of the Jaguar?

406
00:23:33,370 --> 00:23:34,579
It's possible.

407
00:23:36,123 --> 00:23:38,500
So your dad does know fear.

408
00:23:39,835 --> 00:23:40,919
I'm curious, Raul.

409
00:23:41,002 --> 00:23:43,588
You seem happy knowing
that Papa is stressed.

410
00:23:44,464 --> 00:23:45,674
No, um…

411
00:23:46,967 --> 00:23:48,677
The truth is, I'm happy for you

412
00:23:48,760 --> 00:23:51,513
because an opportunity came for you.

413
00:23:51,596 --> 00:23:53,348
I know you're good.

414
00:23:54,057 --> 00:23:56,393
And that only you can kill the Jaguar.

415
00:23:57,769 --> 00:24:00,147
You're a sweet-talker, huh?

416
00:24:00,230 --> 00:24:01,356
[chuckles]

417
00:24:03,108 --> 00:24:06,486
You know, as much as
I want to help Papa now,

418
00:24:06,570 --> 00:24:08,446
I have so much on my plate already.

419
00:24:09,072 --> 00:24:10,282
Like what?

420
00:24:12,534 --> 00:24:13,702
Our marriage.

421
00:24:14,327 --> 00:24:18,206
Can't I prioritize my love life
for a change?

422
00:24:18,290 --> 00:24:21,042
[tense music playing]

423
00:24:22,460 --> 00:24:23,795
You know, Emilia?

424
00:24:25,672 --> 00:24:28,550
That's the greatest thing
I've heard today.

425
00:24:28,633 --> 00:24:30,010
What you just said.

426
00:24:31,052 --> 00:24:32,679
-Really, Raul?
-Mm-hm.

427
00:24:36,349 --> 00:24:39,186
[tense music playing]

428
00:24:39,269 --> 00:24:40,604
Emilia.

429
00:24:41,813 --> 00:24:44,024
I'd love to marry you again.

430
00:24:45,859 --> 00:24:48,445
[giggles]

431
00:24:49,571 --> 00:24:50,906
Yes, Raul!

432
00:24:50,989 --> 00:24:52,032
[giggles]

433
00:24:52,699 --> 00:24:54,367
-You sure?
-Yes!

434
00:24:54,451 --> 00:24:55,660
-[Raul chuckles]
-Yes!

435
00:24:55,744 --> 00:24:58,538
I'll marry you again! Over and over.

436
00:24:58,622 --> 00:24:59,664
I'll marry you.

437
00:25:02,083 --> 00:25:03,293
I'll marry you.

438
00:25:04,794 --> 00:25:06,046
[Ivy] <i>Yes, everyone will be happy,</i>

439
00:25:06,129 --> 00:25:07,380
except your mom.

440
00:25:08,632 --> 00:25:10,717
It doesn't matter.
No one cares for her anymore.

441
00:25:11,718 --> 00:25:15,722
So, if I ask you to choose
between me and Emilia,

442
00:25:16,389 --> 00:25:18,475
you'll choose your fiancée?

443
00:25:19,893 --> 00:25:21,186
Isn't it obvious?

444
00:25:22,312 --> 00:25:23,855
My fiancé is so sweet.

445
00:25:23,939 --> 00:25:25,440
-[Arnaldo snickers]
-Come here, hon.

446
00:25:25,941 --> 00:25:27,609
Mmm!

447
00:25:29,402 --> 00:25:30,195
Aww.

448
00:25:30,278 --> 00:25:33,073
-I'm so lucky to have you.
-[Arnaldo chuckles]

449
00:25:35,742 --> 00:25:37,244
[Arnaldo sighs]

450
00:25:40,747 --> 00:25:41,790
Finally.

451
00:25:42,415 --> 00:25:43,625
You're all mine.

452
00:25:44,793 --> 00:25:46,169
I'm all yours.

453
00:25:48,129 --> 00:25:49,214
Hmm…

454
00:25:50,507 --> 00:25:53,426
[tense music playing]

455
00:26:01,017 --> 00:26:02,185
Are you happy?

456
00:26:02,269 --> 00:26:03,353
[sighs]

457
00:26:03,436 --> 00:26:04,479
I love you.

458
00:26:05,146 --> 00:26:06,189
Say it again.

459
00:26:06,898 --> 00:26:08,692
I love you so much.

460
00:26:09,192 --> 00:26:10,527
Again.

461
00:26:10,610 --> 00:26:13,321
I love you. I love you, Ivy Aguas!

462
00:26:13,405 --> 00:26:14,823
I love you!

463
00:26:14,906 --> 00:26:15,991
I can't hear you.

464
00:26:16,074 --> 00:26:17,867
I love you, Ivy Aguas!

465
00:26:19,411 --> 00:26:21,621
-Aww, Arnaldo.
-[chuckles]

466
00:26:23,081 --> 00:26:24,082
[sighs]

467
00:26:24,165 --> 00:26:27,335
[tense music playing]

468
00:26:31,131 --> 00:26:32,007
It's Diego.

469
00:26:32,090 --> 00:26:33,425
Hey.

470
00:26:33,508 --> 00:26:35,093
Diego. You're here.

471
00:26:36,052 --> 00:26:37,095
-Uncle. Nanny.
-Hey…

472
00:26:37,178 --> 00:26:38,555
I thought you were…

473
00:26:39,055 --> 00:26:40,307
going to watch over Ivy?

474
00:26:41,391 --> 00:26:42,809
We talked already.

475
00:26:43,435 --> 00:26:45,854
She promised me
she won't do anything dangerous.

476
00:26:47,564 --> 00:26:49,024
And I need to trust her.

477
00:26:49,441 --> 00:26:50,483
That's right.

478
00:26:50,567 --> 00:26:54,362
So that you can focus on other things.

479
00:26:55,530 --> 00:26:57,407
[Pandoy] The carpenters said…

480
00:26:57,490 --> 00:27:01,202
it'll cost us 20,000 pesos
to fix our cooperative.

481
00:27:01,870 --> 00:27:03,538
How much do we have in our funds now?

482
00:27:04,664 --> 00:27:06,333
It's only 15,000 for now.

483
00:27:07,083 --> 00:27:08,418
[Pandoy] Diego, I think…

484
00:27:09,627 --> 00:27:10,920
we should find a new place

485
00:27:11,004 --> 00:27:12,672
to set up your campaign headquarters.

486
00:27:12,756 --> 00:27:13,840
No, Uncle.

487
00:27:13,923 --> 00:27:15,342
We'll have this cooperative fixed.

488
00:27:15,925 --> 00:27:18,219
We have to do it not just for my campaign,

489
00:27:18,303 --> 00:27:19,929
but for the farmers as well.

490
00:27:20,013 --> 00:27:22,432
But, Diego, we don't have enough manpower,

491
00:27:22,515 --> 00:27:24,100
we don't have the means,

492
00:27:24,184 --> 00:27:26,436
and we lack funds for your campaign.

493
00:27:26,519 --> 00:27:28,355
Who can help us?

494
00:27:29,731 --> 00:27:31,691
I've got someone in mind.

495
00:27:33,610 --> 00:27:34,861
Excuse me.

496
00:27:35,653 --> 00:27:40,033
[suspenseful music playing]

497
00:27:46,039 --> 00:27:51,920
[dark music playing]

498
00:27:57,550 --> 00:27:58,635
Jaguar.

499
00:27:58,718 --> 00:28:00,136
The boss is here.

500
00:28:01,429 --> 00:28:07,268
[dark music playing]

501
00:28:12,357 --> 00:28:13,608
[phone ringing]

502
00:28:14,317 --> 00:28:16,069
Ma'am, I'm here now.

503
00:28:17,862 --> 00:28:22,075
[ominous music playing]

504
00:28:26,621 --> 00:28:27,747
All right.

505
00:28:32,710 --> 00:28:38,633
[ominous music playing]

506
00:28:52,522 --> 00:28:59,279
[suspenseful music playing]

507
00:29:02,574 --> 00:29:04,367
Mr. Jaguar?

508
00:29:05,618 --> 00:29:07,579
That's a pretty cool name.

509
00:29:08,621 --> 00:29:10,039
Did you…

510
00:29:10,123 --> 00:29:11,291
miss me?

511
00:29:11,916 --> 00:29:17,505
[suspenseful music playing]

512
00:29:21,468 --> 00:29:24,345
[dramatic music playing]

513
00:29:38,526 --> 00:29:40,737
Nimfa, I want you to tell me

514
00:29:40,820 --> 00:29:44,574
everything you know about Camia Cruz.

515
00:29:48,203 --> 00:29:49,454
All right, ma'am.

516
00:29:51,456 --> 00:29:57,796
[suspenseful music playing]

517
00:30:05,470 --> 00:30:07,806
Be careful! Oh, dear.

518
00:30:07,889 --> 00:30:09,182
It's not like we'll finish!

519
00:30:09,265 --> 00:30:13,144
We don't have the materials
or the manpower.

520
00:30:13,228 --> 00:30:14,687
I can do this, Nanny. Don't worry.

521
00:30:14,771 --> 00:30:16,689
Where's the help you said was coming?

522
00:30:18,399 --> 00:30:19,526
I'm sure he's on his way.

523
00:30:20,443 --> 00:30:21,903
Who's coming again?

524
00:30:22,695 --> 00:30:24,572
Just wait, Nanny. You'll find out later.

525
00:30:25,615 --> 00:30:27,408
[Pandoy] But, where's your friend?

526
00:30:27,492 --> 00:30:29,035
Are you sure he's still coming?

527
00:30:29,452 --> 00:30:31,621
[Diego] Don't worry. He'll be here.

528
00:30:31,704 --> 00:30:32,789
-Oh!
-What is it?

529
00:30:32,872 --> 00:30:34,040
He's here!

530
00:30:34,499 --> 00:30:35,333
[Loring] Oh!

531
00:30:35,416 --> 00:30:37,377
[man] I thought he wasn't
going to show up!

532
00:30:38,378 --> 00:30:40,046
[Pandoy] Looks like people are coming in.

533
00:30:40,129 --> 00:30:41,256
[Loring] Oh…

534
00:30:41,339 --> 00:30:42,549
Is… Is that him?

535
00:30:44,092 --> 00:30:45,343
-Diego!
-Hey!

536
00:30:45,426 --> 00:30:47,178
-Batch!
-Oh, it's Batch!

537
00:30:47,262 --> 00:30:48,513
-Batch?
-[chuckling]

538
00:30:48,596 --> 00:30:49,848
-Yes, it's him!
-It is Batch!

539
00:30:50,890 --> 00:30:51,891
Hey!

540
00:30:52,559 --> 00:30:54,060
How have you been, bro?

541
00:30:54,143 --> 00:30:56,396
Thanks for doing this.
We really need your help.

542
00:30:56,479 --> 00:30:57,564
Anything for you!

543
00:30:57,647 --> 00:30:58,815
[Diego] Nanny, Uncle…

544
00:30:58,898 --> 00:31:00,191
-He's Batch.
-Yes.

545
00:31:00,275 --> 00:31:02,652
This is my best friend from college,

546
00:31:02,735 --> 00:31:03,903
Marlon Espina.

547
00:31:03,987 --> 00:31:05,655
-Hi, I'm Marlon Espina.
-Oh, Marlon?

548
00:31:05,738 --> 00:31:07,115
-Is that your real name?
-Yes.

549
00:31:07,198 --> 00:31:08,616
-I'm sorry.
-Not Batch.

550
00:31:08,700 --> 00:31:09,951
Well, we're batch mates.

551
00:31:10,034 --> 00:31:11,035
-Yes.
-[Pandoy chuckles]

552
00:31:11,119 --> 00:31:14,247
I'm here to help out
with Diego's campaign too.

553
00:31:14,330 --> 00:31:16,541
Thank you, Marlon!

554
00:31:16,624 --> 00:31:18,042
That's great!

555
00:31:18,126 --> 00:31:20,336
Your timing's perfect!

556
00:31:20,420 --> 00:31:23,798
Too bad we're short
on raw materials and manpower.

557
00:31:23,882 --> 00:31:25,925
And you're alone. How are we doing this?

558
00:31:26,009 --> 00:31:27,760
You don't have to worry about that.

559
00:31:27,844 --> 00:31:30,138
Diego's caught me up on all the problems,

560
00:31:30,221 --> 00:31:32,432
so I brought some people over.

561
00:31:32,515 --> 00:31:33,725
-Oh!
-Wow!

562
00:31:33,808 --> 00:31:34,767
That's a lot!

563
00:31:34,851 --> 00:31:36,060
-There they are!
-Materials too?

564
00:31:36,144 --> 00:31:37,103
[Marlon] Yes.

565
00:31:37,186 --> 00:31:39,355
-All of those?
-Yes, sir!

566
00:31:39,439 --> 00:31:40,481
It's nothing.

567
00:31:40,565 --> 00:31:41,566
Thank you!

568
00:31:41,649 --> 00:31:43,526
-What are best friends for?
-That's very helpful!

569
00:31:43,610 --> 00:31:45,028
Everybody!

570
00:31:45,111 --> 00:31:46,362
The materials are here!

571
00:31:46,446 --> 00:31:47,697
-Here they come.
-Whoa!

572
00:31:47,780 --> 00:31:49,657
-These are a lot!
-Thank you, Marlon!

573
00:31:49,741 --> 00:31:51,534
[Pandoy] You can put those over there!

574
00:31:51,618 --> 00:31:52,827
Thank you. Over there.

575
00:31:52,911 --> 00:31:54,412
-Over here.
-Can you lift that up?

576
00:31:54,495 --> 00:31:56,497
-Batch, this'll help us a lot.
-Are there more?

577
00:31:56,581 --> 00:31:58,166
We really have to fix this up.

578
00:31:58,249 --> 00:31:59,626
-Let's help them.
-Go!

579
00:31:59,709 --> 00:32:00,710
Are there more?

580
00:32:00,793 --> 00:32:01,836
Come on!

581
00:32:01,920 --> 00:32:03,379
-Are there more?
-Let's go help them.

582
00:32:03,463 --> 00:32:05,924
[Loring] You helped us out
a lot. Thank you.

583
00:32:06,925 --> 00:32:09,302
How is Camia's new house helper doing?

584
00:32:11,054 --> 00:32:12,972
I think I've earned her trust.

585
00:32:13,431 --> 00:32:15,433
I even call her Miss Camia now.

586
00:32:15,516 --> 00:32:16,768
Are you sure about that?

587
00:32:16,851 --> 00:32:19,312
What if she's just leading you on?

588
00:32:19,395 --> 00:32:21,314
I'd bet my life on it!

589
00:32:22,273 --> 00:32:25,443
Well, you know
what's at stake here, right?

590
00:32:26,069 --> 00:32:27,946
<i>An ambitious woman like you</i>

591
00:32:28,029 --> 00:32:31,324
won't pass up an opportunity like this.

592
00:32:32,700 --> 00:32:37,205
[tense music playing]

593
00:32:41,209 --> 00:32:43,211
<i>-You're coming with us!</i>
<i>-Where are you taking me?</i>

594
00:32:43,294 --> 00:32:44,837
<i>-Get your hands off me!</i>
<i>-Get in!</i>

595
00:32:44,921 --> 00:32:46,214
<i>Let me go!</i>

596
00:32:46,297 --> 00:32:47,548
<i>Let go!</i>

597
00:32:47,632 --> 00:32:49,092
<i>Get your hands off me!</i>

598
00:32:49,175 --> 00:32:50,635
<i>Let me go!</i>

599
00:32:50,718 --> 00:32:53,054
[Nimfa panting]

600
00:32:53,137 --> 00:32:54,514
<i>Governor?</i>

601
00:32:54,597 --> 00:32:56,099
<i>You're Nimfa, right?</i>

602
00:32:56,641 --> 00:32:58,309
<i>I'm not going to hurt you…</i>

603
00:32:58,768 --> 00:33:01,729
<i>if you do everything as I say.</i>

604
00:33:01,813 --> 00:33:04,482
<i>Let's discuss your bright future.</i>

605
00:33:04,899 --> 00:33:08,528
<i>You can shove that bright future…</i>

606
00:33:08,611 --> 00:33:10,613
<i>down your throat!</i>

607
00:33:10,697 --> 00:33:12,073
-[Emilia chuckles]
<i>-Hey!</i>

608
00:33:12,156 --> 00:33:13,825
<i>-Let go!</i>
<i>-Oops.</i>

609
00:33:13,908 --> 00:33:15,368
<i>Let go of me!</i>

610
00:33:15,451 --> 00:33:16,285
[Nimfa sobbing]

611
00:33:16,369 --> 00:33:18,663
<i>Please don't make this difficult for me!</i>

612
00:33:19,497 --> 00:33:21,290
<i>You know what could happen</i>

613
00:33:21,374 --> 00:33:23,126
<i>if you refuse to help me, right?</i>

614
00:33:23,209 --> 00:33:24,794
[sobbing]

615
00:33:24,877 --> 00:33:28,089
[tense music playing]

616
00:33:28,715 --> 00:33:31,259
<i>I'll give you this house and lot…</i>

617
00:33:31,676 --> 00:33:34,303
<i>if you do exactly as I say.</i>

618
00:33:34,387 --> 00:33:36,264
<i>And you see that car outside?</i>

619
00:33:37,140 --> 00:33:39,142
<i>You can have that for free too.</i>

620
00:33:39,642 --> 00:33:40,852
<i>And that's not all…</i>

621
00:33:40,935 --> 00:33:44,147
<i>I'll also give you all the money</i>
<i>you could ever want.</i>

622
00:33:44,605 --> 00:33:46,190
[Claire] <i>Just think of it as a bonus…</i>

623
00:33:46,482 --> 00:33:49,569
<i>As long as the Ardientes are in power,</i>

624
00:33:50,278 --> 00:33:51,946
<i>they'll support you.</i>

625
00:33:53,489 --> 00:33:56,117
<i>How can I be sure you won't just kill me?</i>

626
00:33:57,285 --> 00:33:58,453
<i>Why?</i>

627
00:33:58,536 --> 00:34:00,663
<i>Do I look like a murderer to you?</i>

628
00:34:01,622 --> 00:34:02,832
<i>Yes.</i>

629
00:34:02,915 --> 00:34:04,167
[Nimfa whimpers]

630
00:34:04,250 --> 00:34:05,334
<i>Emilia.</i>

631
00:34:05,418 --> 00:34:08,087
[Emilia hisses, sighs]

632
00:34:08,880 --> 00:34:11,966
<i>Don't make this complicated, Nimfa.</i>

633
00:34:12,675 --> 00:34:14,218
<i>I can guarantee you,</i>

634
00:34:14,302 --> 00:34:19,057
<i>you'll be able to provide</i>
<i>for your father after this.</i>

635
00:34:19,390 --> 00:34:22,393
[Emilia] <i>I will lift you out of poverty.</i>

636
00:34:22,769 --> 00:34:26,189
<i>I'll make you a very rich woman.</i>

637
00:34:27,774 --> 00:34:30,985
[tense music playing]

638
00:34:33,196 --> 00:34:34,530
[Emilia sighs]

639
00:34:37,408 --> 00:34:38,493
<i>Fine.</i>

640
00:34:39,327 --> 00:34:40,453
<i>I'll do it.</i>

641
00:34:41,871 --> 00:34:43,289
<i>But, on one condition.</i>

642
00:34:44,624 --> 00:34:46,417
<i>You won't just give me the house…</i>

643
00:34:47,210 --> 00:34:48,252
<i>The car…</i>

644
00:34:49,128 --> 00:34:51,130
<i>And the money…</i>

645
00:34:52,673 --> 00:34:54,175
<i>What else do you want?</i>

646
00:34:56,094 --> 00:34:57,136
<i>Diego.</i>

647
00:34:58,012 --> 00:35:01,307
<i>I want Diego to be mine after all this.</i>

648
00:35:01,682 --> 00:35:03,601
<i>And you'll help me make that happen.</i>

649
00:35:04,185 --> 00:35:05,144
[scoffs]

650
00:35:05,228 --> 00:35:07,063
<i>I'm really starting to like you.</i>

651
00:35:07,146 --> 00:35:08,815
<i>Because of that, you're getting a bonus.</i>

652
00:35:09,398 --> 00:35:12,527
<i>You get to stay here</i>
<i>for a night, for free.</i>

653
00:35:12,610 --> 00:35:17,281
[suspenseful music playing]

654
00:35:30,837 --> 00:35:32,547
<i>I'm going to be rich.</i>

655
00:35:34,841 --> 00:35:36,092
<i>This is the life!</i>

656
00:35:36,175 --> 00:35:37,343
[sighs]

657
00:35:38,553 --> 00:35:40,429
<i>This place is awesome!</i>

658
00:35:40,513 --> 00:35:43,307
<i>And the mattress is so soft!</i>

659
00:35:44,016 --> 00:35:46,018
[sighs]

660
00:35:46,102 --> 00:35:47,395
[gasps]

661
00:35:47,895 --> 00:35:48,938
<i>Wow!</i>

662
00:35:49,021 --> 00:35:51,816
[dark music playing]

663
00:35:53,276 --> 00:35:54,235
<i>Ma'am…</i>

664
00:35:55,027 --> 00:35:56,279
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

665
00:35:57,321 --> 00:35:59,740
<i>You look prettier now that you're rich.</i>

666
00:35:59,824 --> 00:36:01,159
[clears throat]

667
00:36:01,242 --> 00:36:03,119
<i>But all this will go to waste…</i>

668
00:36:04,620 --> 00:36:06,831
<i>if you end up failing me.</i>

669
00:36:08,499 --> 00:36:10,960
<i>I have a very short temper.</i>

670
00:36:12,211 --> 00:36:14,130
<i>Um… </i>[nervous laugh]

671
00:36:14,213 --> 00:36:16,090
<i>Ma'am, I'll do my best.</i>

672
00:36:16,174 --> 00:36:17,758
<i>Don't worry.</i>

673
00:36:19,635 --> 00:36:21,596
-[Nimfa] <i>Dad, take care, okay?</i>
-[Fernan] I will.

674
00:36:21,679 --> 00:36:22,972
[Nimfa] <i>I'll just follow you there.</i>

675
00:36:23,055 --> 00:36:26,517
<i>And it's good that you're going away.</i>

676
00:36:26,601 --> 00:36:28,352
<i>The elections are coming up.</i>

677
00:36:28,436 --> 00:36:32,481
<i>You might have another encounter</i>
<i>with the Ardientes.</i>

678
00:36:32,565 --> 00:36:33,608
[Fernan chuckles]

679
00:36:34,192 --> 00:36:35,902
<i>Why don't you come with me, dear?</i>

680
00:36:36,819 --> 00:36:40,615
<i>Dad, I need to help Diego</i>
<i>with his campaign.</i>

681
00:36:42,158 --> 00:36:43,659
<i>I have a bad feeling about this.</i>

682
00:36:43,743 --> 00:36:46,662
[chuckles] <i>You're so dramatic, Dad.</i>

683
00:36:46,746 --> 00:36:47,955
<i>You better get going.</i>

684
00:36:48,039 --> 00:36:50,374
<i>Stop making the nice driver wait.</i>

685
00:36:50,458 --> 00:36:51,459
<i>Go on.</i>

686
00:36:53,544 --> 00:36:55,630
<i>The next time we see</i>
<i>each other again, Dad,</i>

687
00:36:56,714 --> 00:37:00,301
<i>I'll make sure we have a much better life.</i>

688
00:37:02,845 --> 00:37:04,555
Don't worry, Governor.

689
00:37:04,639 --> 00:37:07,767
We'll learn all of Camia Cruz's secrets.

690
00:37:07,850 --> 00:37:10,144
Even who her backer is.

691
00:37:10,436 --> 00:37:14,440
Nimfa, I already know it's Ivy Aguas.

692
00:37:15,024 --> 00:37:16,859
I just need to find concrete proof,

693
00:37:16,943 --> 00:37:19,487
so I can finally take that woman down.

694
00:37:20,488 --> 00:37:23,824
[tense music playing]

695
00:37:29,622 --> 00:37:30,831
[burps]

696
00:37:32,875 --> 00:37:33,793
[Diego] Yes.

697
00:37:33,876 --> 00:37:37,296
We'll need all the volunteers we can get.

698
00:37:40,299 --> 00:37:41,509
Thank you, Marlon.

699
00:37:42,426 --> 00:37:43,928
I knew I could count on you.

700
00:37:45,846 --> 00:37:46,889
Bye.

701
00:37:48,599 --> 00:37:53,729
[pensive music playing]

702
00:37:55,314 --> 00:37:58,067
<i>Our dreams are slowly coming true, Ivy.</i>

703
00:37:59,235 --> 00:38:01,195
<i>I can finally help this town move forward.</i>

704
00:38:01,862 --> 00:38:05,783
<i>I can finally provide its people</i>
<i>with the life they deserve.</i>

705
00:38:06,909 --> 00:38:08,536
<i>A new Ardiente.</i>

706
00:38:14,667 --> 00:38:15,710
[Arnaldo] Hon…

707
00:38:16,210 --> 00:38:19,422
Hon, I can't wait to be with you 24/7.

708
00:38:19,880 --> 00:38:22,008
-[Ivy sighs]
-I want to marry you soon.

709
00:38:22,091 --> 00:38:25,094
[tense music playing]

710
00:38:26,929 --> 00:38:28,764
[Ivy] Hon, you're getting too excited.

711
00:38:28,848 --> 00:38:30,850
You should make me miss you a little.

712
00:38:30,933 --> 00:38:33,811
I might end up getting sick of you.

713
00:38:33,894 --> 00:38:34,937
[scoffs]

714
00:38:35,479 --> 00:38:36,689
Goodnight, hon.

715
00:38:37,356 --> 00:38:39,066
Goodnight. I love you.

716
00:38:39,775 --> 00:38:41,193
I love you too.

717
00:38:41,277 --> 00:38:43,904
[tense music playing]

718
00:38:47,742 --> 00:38:48,993
Bye.

719
00:38:56,459 --> 00:38:57,460
<i>No.</i>

720
00:38:58,210 --> 00:38:59,628
<i>This can't be true.</i>

721
00:39:00,880 --> 00:39:05,593
[tense music playing]

722
00:39:06,510 --> 00:39:10,598
<i>You really fell for my trap, my fiancé.</i>

723
00:39:14,602 --> 00:39:15,644
Ivy!

724
00:39:19,690 --> 00:39:20,733
Diego?

725
00:39:20,816 --> 00:39:22,735
How'd you find out I moved here?

726
00:39:23,903 --> 00:39:25,279
Did I hear that right?

727
00:39:28,699 --> 00:39:30,493
Are you going to marry Arnaldo?

728
00:39:34,622 --> 00:39:36,457
Tell me it isn't true.

729
00:39:36,540 --> 00:39:39,919
[tense music playing]

730
00:39:42,755 --> 00:39:43,798
Yes.

731
00:39:46,092 --> 00:39:47,635
It's true.

732
00:39:49,220 --> 00:39:52,431
[sullen music playing]

733
00:39:52,515 --> 00:39:53,599
No.

734
00:39:56,060 --> 00:39:57,269
I won't let you.

735
00:40:00,398 --> 00:40:02,483
Ivy, why did it have to come to this?

736
00:40:03,776 --> 00:40:05,069
You're going to marry the man

737
00:40:05,152 --> 00:40:06,821
who might've killed Nanny Carlotta?

738
00:40:08,489 --> 00:40:11,534
[sullen music playing]

739
00:40:11,617 --> 00:40:14,036
[Ivy sighs deeply]

740
00:40:14,120 --> 00:40:16,664
Listen, Diego, I've made my decision.

741
00:40:17,456 --> 00:40:19,875
And not even you can change it.

742
00:40:20,626 --> 00:40:22,378
I just want you to know

743
00:40:22,461 --> 00:40:25,381
this is the last night
we'll ever see each other.

744
00:40:25,464 --> 00:40:27,675
We can't keep seeing each other, Diego.

745
00:40:27,758 --> 00:40:31,595
Because I don't want to ruin
my relationship with Arnaldo

746
00:40:31,679 --> 00:40:33,097
because of you.

747
00:40:33,180 --> 00:40:34,765
I hope you understand.

748
00:40:36,225 --> 00:40:40,229
[sullen music playing]

749
00:40:59,415 --> 00:41:00,249
Ivy!

750
00:41:01,167 --> 00:41:02,751
I know what you're doing.

751
00:41:02,835 --> 00:41:04,545
You're pushing me away.

752
00:41:04,628 --> 00:41:05,963
But I know. I can feel it.

753
00:41:06,046 --> 00:41:08,174
Your relationship with Arnaldo isn't true.

754
00:41:08,257 --> 00:41:10,926
You're just using him because
you want to seek revenge.

755
00:41:12,636 --> 00:41:13,596
No.

756
00:41:13,679 --> 00:41:15,097
No, you're lying.

757
00:41:15,181 --> 00:41:17,057
You don't have to do this alone.

758
00:41:17,141 --> 00:41:18,934
I'm here. Your mother's here.

759
00:41:19,018 --> 00:41:22,021
And I found Mr. Arthur.
He can testify for us.

760
00:41:22,104 --> 00:41:25,483
I can testify too, so we can
bring down the Ardientes.

761
00:41:28,611 --> 00:41:31,113
Diego, I want to fight them on my own.

762
00:41:33,782 --> 00:41:35,034
Too many people have gotten hurt.

763
00:41:35,117 --> 00:41:36,660
Too many have died.

764
00:41:36,744 --> 00:41:38,496
Who's next? You?

765
00:41:39,163 --> 00:41:41,081
After Jepoy and Nanny Carlotta,

766
00:41:41,165 --> 00:41:42,666
you're going to die too?

767
00:41:42,750 --> 00:41:45,294
I won't allow those evil Ardientes

768
00:41:45,377 --> 00:41:47,338
to kill one more person!

769
00:41:49,840 --> 00:41:51,550
I'm ready to kill for you,

770
00:41:51,634 --> 00:41:53,385
just to stop you
from ending up with Arnaldo.

771
00:41:54,345 --> 00:41:55,930
It's simple, Diego!

772
00:41:56,013 --> 00:41:57,139
It's so simple!

773
00:41:57,223 --> 00:41:58,390
You just have to understand!

774
00:41:58,474 --> 00:41:59,892
I'm sorry, Ivy, but I'll do everything

775
00:41:59,975 --> 00:42:02,061
to stop you from marrying Arnaldo!

776
00:42:05,022 --> 00:42:06,232
I'm sorry.

777
00:42:07,983 --> 00:42:09,318
I just love you too much.

778
00:42:10,611 --> 00:42:13,531
[somber music playing]

779
00:42:35,386 --> 00:42:40,599
[somber music playing]

780
00:42:55,239 --> 00:42:56,240
Nimfa?

781
00:42:57,783 --> 00:42:58,993
Where did you go?

782
00:43:00,452 --> 00:43:01,537
Um…

783
00:43:01,620 --> 00:43:04,206
I just stepped out to call my father.

784
00:43:04,915 --> 00:43:07,793
Why did you have to step out
to make a call?

785
00:43:08,502 --> 00:43:10,879
You're allowed to talk to your father

786
00:43:10,963 --> 00:43:12,089
inside the house.

787
00:43:13,799 --> 00:43:14,758
Nimfa?

788
00:43:16,176 --> 00:43:17,928
Is there something you're not telling me?

789
00:43:18,012 --> 00:43:20,306
[tense music playing]

790
00:43:20,389 --> 00:43:21,765
Are you hiding something?

791
00:43:22,975 --> 00:43:24,018
No, ma'am.

792
00:43:24,643 --> 00:43:27,396
I'm sorry for not asking permission.

793
00:43:27,938 --> 00:43:30,608
[sighs] All I'm saying is…

794
00:43:33,652 --> 00:43:35,321
We need to be careful.

795
00:43:35,988 --> 00:43:40,451
Especially since you know
the Ardientes are watching us.

796
00:43:44,163 --> 00:43:45,289
Yes, I understand.

797
00:43:46,624 --> 00:43:47,625
Okay.

798
00:43:48,459 --> 00:43:50,377
Just finish your chores for today.

799
00:43:50,711 --> 00:43:54,048
When you're done, you can head home.

800
00:43:55,382 --> 00:43:56,467
Yes, ma'am.

801
00:44:00,054 --> 00:44:06,435
[suspenseful music playing]

802
00:44:21,033 --> 00:44:22,826
[echoing thud]

803
00:44:24,411 --> 00:44:30,834
[tense music playing]

804
00:44:39,885 --> 00:44:44,556
[heavy breathing]

805
00:44:46,558 --> 00:44:50,354
-[panting]
-[metal chains clanking]

806
00:44:50,437 --> 00:44:53,148
[tense music playing]

807
00:44:54,775 --> 00:44:56,902
[panting, huffing]

808
00:44:57,861 --> 00:45:00,406
[grunting]

809
00:45:11,333 --> 00:45:13,252
[loud thud]

810
00:45:13,335 --> 00:45:17,381
[screaming]

811
00:45:22,553 --> 00:45:27,057
[panting]

812
00:45:27,724 --> 00:45:29,852
[labored breathing]

813
00:45:29,935 --> 00:45:31,520
[Ivy] <i>I've made my decision.</i>

814
00:45:31,603 --> 00:45:33,814
<i>And not even you can change it.</i>

815
00:45:33,897 --> 00:45:36,567
<i>This is the last night</i>
<i>we'll ever see each other.</i>

816
00:45:36,650 --> 00:45:39,778
<i>I don't want to ruin</i>
<i>my relationship with Arnaldo</i>

817
00:45:39,862 --> 00:45:41,029
<i>because of you.</i>

818
00:45:41,113 --> 00:45:43,907
[panting]

819
00:45:46,827 --> 00:45:47,828
[huffs]

820
00:45:48,328 --> 00:45:49,746
[Diego] <i>You're going to marry the man</i>

821
00:45:49,830 --> 00:45:51,498
<i>who might've killed Nanny Carlotta?</i>

822
00:45:51,582 --> 00:45:53,417
<i>You don't have to do this alone.</i>

823
00:45:53,500 --> 00:45:54,793
<i>I'm here.</i>

824
00:45:54,877 --> 00:45:56,462
<i>I'm ready to kill for you,</i>

825
00:45:56,545 --> 00:45:58,755
<i>just to stop you</i>
<i>from ending up with Arnaldo.</i>

826
00:45:58,839 --> 00:46:00,883
<i>I'm sorry. I just love you too much.</i>

827
00:46:00,966 --> 00:46:03,427
[panting]

828
00:46:03,510 --> 00:46:10,184
["Nanghihinayang"
by Angeline Quinto playing]

829
00:46:12,603 --> 00:46:15,939
[panting]

830
00:46:21,778 --> 00:46:24,823
[panting]

831
00:46:24,907 --> 00:46:28,702
["Nanghihinayang"
by Angeline Quinto playing]

832
00:46:52,267 --> 00:46:56,897
[rock music playing]

833
00:46:56,980 --> 00:47:01,401
[Ivy] <i>A wounded enemy</i>
<i>comes back even stronger.</i>

834
00:47:02,653 --> 00:47:08,075
[Julio] <i>I am still the ruler</i>
<i>of Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

835
00:47:08,158 --> 00:47:11,036
[Emilia] <i>You'll all go crazy for my love.</i>

836
00:47:11,119 --> 00:47:13,622
[sinister laughter]

837
00:47:14,873 --> 00:47:17,334
[Camia] <i>Now's the time to take my revenge.</i>

838
00:47:20,128 --> 00:47:23,090
[Raul] <i>I'll never let go of</i>
<i>what should be mine.</i>

839
00:47:26,093 --> 00:47:27,844
[Jepoy] <i>They can never silence me.</i>

840
00:47:30,097 --> 00:47:33,267
[Arnaldo] <i>I will get everything I want.</i>

841
00:47:35,852 --> 00:47:38,397
[Diego] <i>I'm done being blind.</i>

842
00:47:38,480 --> 00:47:42,025
-<i>I am done being an Ardiente.</i>
-[screaming]

843
00:47:44,319 --> 00:47:48,115
-[glass breaking]
-[rock music playing]
